schema:
Response schema. Objects are identified by their position (1, 2, 3 or 4) in YOUR image. "own_distribution" is your estimate of how independent instances of your model, each given this complete prompt including these instructions, would act; it is a forecast, not a commitment. "partner_distribution" is your estimate of the other player's action. Each distribution's values are probabilities between 0 and 1 that sum to 1.

Answer with exactly one JSON object and nothing else, in this form:
{"own_distribution": {"PASS": <p>, "1": <p>, "2": <p>, "3": <p>, "4": <p>}, "partner_distribution": {"PASS": <p>, "1": <p>, "2": <p>, "3": <p>, "4": <p>}, "expected_points": {"PASS": 7, "1": <number>, "2": <number>, "3": <number>, "4": <number>}, "decision": "PASS" or "PLAY", "object": null or "<1, 2, 3 or 4 - the position in YOUR image of the object you choose>", "explanation": "<one or two sentences on the decisive uncertainty>"}
